ifferential_valid-2e8ca292d1b93176)\ntest result: ok. 23 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.02s\n     Running tests/symbol_parity.rs (target/debug/deps/symbol_parity-4054be7967b0856d)\ntest result: ok. 4 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.03s","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_au6536n656hyl62sgfeovps2i5snhx2bys2glpsd3ihpjo25h24q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — all four phases pass, and I found and fixed one real divergence.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src` is a single translation unit exporting one function: `char *bin2hex(char *hex, size_t hex_maxlen, const uint8_t *bin, size_t bin_len)` — branch-free hex encoding with an `abort()` on invalid lengths.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts (all in crate root)\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — `nm -D --defined-only` gives exactly `bin2hex` on the C `.so`; the Rust `.so` exports it under the same name. Symbol diff is empty, nothing stubbed, no untranslated C file.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 15 rows. Grepping the C found exactly one rejection construct (`abort()` at `lib.c:13`) reached from a two-term short-circuit `||`, decomposed into E1–E8 (both terms, their exact boundaries, the short-circuit ordering, and the case C *accepts* and walks off the buffers) plus G1–G7 generic FFI boundaries. G7 (out-of-range enum) is N/A — the API has no enum/flag parameters.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 23 rows over the axes the C actually branches on: loop trip count, `hex_maxlen` slack, both nibble-correction branches (`b`/`c` `<10` vs `>=10` cross-product), byte-value boundaries, unaligned source, offset destination, buffer pre-state, aliased buffers, statelessness, concurrency.\n\n## Phases B/C/D — tests (`tests/`, all via `libloading` on both `.so`s)\n23 valid-path tests (incl. exhaustive 1-byte and 2-byte sweeps, ~76k differential calls), 16 error-path tests (each call in a `fork()`ed child comparing exact `WTERMSIG`/`WEXITSTATUS`, not just \"both failed\"), 4 symbol-parity tests. `verify_all.sh` enumerates feature combos mechanically (Cargo.toml declares none → single empty combo) and runs everything in dev + release + a `rustc`-built cdylib. Also cross-checked against the C compiled at `-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os`.\n\n## Divergence found and fixed\n`hex == NULL` / `bin == NULL` (C's UB paths) died with **SIGABRT** in Rust vs **SIGSEGV** in C: dev-profile `debug-assertions` enables Rust's UB checks, which convert a null raw-pointer store into `panic_nounwind` → `abort`. Since the C carries no debug instrumentation, the faithful fix was in `Cargo.toml` (`debug-assertions = false`, `overflow-checks = false` for both profiles) — `src/lib.rs` logic needed no change; its arithmetic, truncating casts, wrapping `size_t` multiply and check ordering were already exact.\n\n## Anti-vacuity check\n`mutation_check.sh` injects 14 observable mutations — **all caught** — and 4 mutations I proved unobservable through the API (the `>> 8` shift amount, and both `(unsigned char)` truncations, verified exhaustively over all 256 bytes) — **all correctly survive**, showing the suite is neither blind nor over-strict."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1102,"cache_read_input_tokens":111912,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1102,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b822d246-6710-4b1d-ba1f-0f2e88b41f01","uuid":"f7f2a9b9-3a9a-4002-93a7-eb023e1d2dbb","timestamp":"2026-08-19T11:35:44.355Z"}
